  "question": {
    "text": "<p>India&#39;s Mangalyan was sent to the Mars by launching it into a transfer orbit EOM around the sun. It leaves the earth at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> and meets Mars at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>. If the semi-major axis of Earth&#39;s orbit is <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>a</mtext> <mtext>e</mtext> </msub> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>1.5</mtext> <mo>&#215;</mo> <mn>1</mn> <msup> <mn>0</mn> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </msup> <mtext>m</mtext> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;, that of Mar&#39;s orbit <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>a</mtext> <mtext>m</mtext> </msub> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>2.28</mtext> <mo>&#215;</mo> <mn>1</mn> <msup> <mn>0</mn> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </msup> <mtext>m</mtext> </mrow> </math>,&nbsp;taking Kepler&#39;s laws, give the estimate of time for Mangalyan to reach Mars from Earth.<br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0183_954c4019ff32.png\" style=\"width: 234px; height: 250px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
